# Phantom Fudge TODO Index

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Entire v1 lifecycle
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Create a complete, evidence-backed Windows 11 speaker-notes application, starting with a
capture proof rather than assuming a window can be universally undetectable.

## Current state

- Implementation authorized October 8. Local experimental implementation is now in progress.
- User approved Windows 11 first with Teams, Zoom, Google Meet, and OBS qualified separately.
- WPF/C#/.NET10 now uses owner-requested background translucency; four-product qualification still blocks release.
- Live meeting-output transcription19 and native Python runtime22 are required; Docker20 is deferred until last.
- Local synthetic GDI/UI/speech evidence and approved hardware-loopback recognition exist.
- No four-product qualification, actual Docker execution, owner UX acceptance, commit, push or public release.
- WORKFLOWS statuses describe authored procedures, not app execution.
